"closed_at":"2026-10-16T16:38:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124497","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124497","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124497.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124497.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-16T16:38:11Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nFixes #124407.\r\n\r\nFound this while working on a project. `RenderingDevice` only adds the allocation size of textures it allocates, but subtracts it for every texture it frees. Vulkan and D3D12 return 0 for views and imported textures, but Metal returned the size of the underlying texture, so 2D textures with an sRGB view were subtracted twice and the counter wrapped around. Metal now returns 0 for those too.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nTested on an M1 with the issue's case and the snippet from my comment there. The counter comes back to where it started on Metal now, Vulkan is unchanged.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repit